Package: empiricaloptions
Type: Package
Title: Empirical 'Martingale' Option Pricing from Historical Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Thierry", "Moudiki", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "thierry.moudiki@gmail.com")
Description: Prices European and arithmetic Asian options directly from a single
    historical price series, with no option-market calibration input. An AR(1)
    filter removes linear predictability from discounted log-prices, a stationary
    block bootstrap (Politis and Romano, 1994) resamples the residuals to preserve
    dependence beyond the mean, and a Duan-Simonato (1998) scalar correction
    enforces the martingale condition required by the Fundamental Theorem of Asset
    Pricing. Intended for underlyings with no quoted option market to calibrate
    against (private indices, embedded insurance options, participation
    certificates).
License: BSD_3_clause + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
LazyData: true
Depends: R (>= 3.5)
Imports: tseries, stats
